<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="privacy_policy_section">
    <div class="privacy_policy_section_inside">
        <h1 class="privacy_policy_heading">Vesopa EPOS Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            This policy explains what cookies and similar technologies
            <%= CONTACT.company %> uses on <%= SITE_URL.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '') %>, why we use
            them, and how you control them. It sits alongside our
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy_item_heading">1. What cookies are</h2>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            A cookie is a small text file a website stores on your device so it can recognise
            you on your next request — to keep you signed in, remember your basket, or count
            visits. This policy also covers similar technologies such as
            <code>localStorage</code>, which we use to remember your cookie choice.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy_item_heading">2. The cookies we use</h2>

        <h3 class="privacy_item_heading">Strictly necessary — always on</h3>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            These make the site work. Without them you could not sign in to the admin panel
            or complete a checkout, so they are set without consent, as the law allows.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Session cookie</b> — keeps you signed in to the admin panel. Expires when
                you sign out or the session ends.</li>
            <li><b>Checkout state</b> — remembers which plan you selected while you complete
                payment.</li>
            <li><b>PayPal</b> — set by PayPal when you pay, to process the transaction and
                prevent fraud.</li>
            <li><b>vesopa_cookie_consent</b> — a <code>localStorage</code> entry recording the
                choice you made here, so we stop asking. Kept for 12 months.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="privacy_item_heading">Analytics — optional</h3>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            Aggregated statistics about which pages are viewed and where visitors leave, so we
            know what to improve. We do not use these to identify you, and we do not sell the
            data. Off unless you turn them on.
        </p>

        <h3 class="privacy_item_heading">Support &amp; marketing — optional</h3>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            Would cover live chat and measuring which campaigns bring businesses to us.
            Off unless you turn them on.
        </p>

        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            <b>We currently use no analytics, advertising or third-party tracking cookies at
            all.</b> The optional categories above are listed so the choice is already yours
            if we add any — and nothing in either category will load unless you have allowed
            it first. If that changes we will update this policy and ask you again.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy_item_heading">3. Changing your mind</h2>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            You can change or withdraw your choice at any time using
            <a href="#" data-cc="open">Cookie Settings</a>, also linked in the footer of every
            page. Withdrawing consent is as easy as giving it, and takes effect immediately.
            We ask again after 12 months, and whenever the cookies we use change.
        </p>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking strictly
            necessary cookies will stop parts of the site — sign-in and checkout — from
            working.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy_item_heading">4. Cookies in the Vesopa EPOS software</h2>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            This policy covers our public website. The Vesopa EPOS till application and the
            Back Office are business tools you sign in to; they use a session token to keep
            you signed in and store your terminal's settings locally on the device. They carry
            no analytics, advertising or third-party tracking cookies.
        </p>

        <h2 class="privacy_item_heading">5. Contact us</h2>
        <p class="privacy_item_sub_heading">
            Questions about this policy, or a request about your data, can go to
            <a href="mailto:<%= CONTACT.support_email %>"><%= CONTACT.support_email %></a> or
            <a href="tel:<%= CONTACT.emergency_phone_e164 %>"><%= CONTACT.emergency_phone %></a>.
            <%= CONTACT.company %>, <%= CONTACT.address_line1 %>, <%= CONTACT.address_line2 %>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
